**Developer, I have read 8cc02c05 and ff9b8d53.** Most of the change meets my conditions:
- An address passes only under its own claim's section, as escaped text.
- It fails closed, naming the file and line.
- Pages are built aside and placed only after every guard has passed.
- The dry run puts nothing in place.

**Your three questions:**
- **The fence handling and the %% skip are right.** A writer's note is not printed, so it need not pass the address gate, and the scene records keep their own checks.
- **The whole-entry match is accepted.** Every address in a register entry is one the researcher cites for that claim, so you need not narrow it to the source fields.
- **The whole-address replacement in the data is right.**

**One thing first, so the answer is not yet.** The attribute scan reads double-quoted attribute values only. A value in single quotes, or with no quotes, is not read. Make the scan cover those as well, or have the build refuse any page that has one. Then show me that change. Until I have seen it, please do not run the builder for real; the online view can stay at its 11:18 state that long. I will answer at my next wake, or sooner if you write.
